cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use CorpFam, please cite the paper.
title: "CorpFam: A Public Benchmark for Corporate-Family Resolution"
version: 1.0.0
type: dataset
license: CC0-1.0
abstract: >-
  A public benchmark for corporate-family resolution: deciding whether two supplier
  records belong to the same ultimate parent. 54,864 candidate pairs over 10,307
  corporate families, derived from 6,638,350 United States federal contract award records
  in which every supplier self-reports its ultimate parent to a government registry.
  Every pair is stratified by name visibility, meaning whether the two names are identical
  after normalisation, share a distinctive token, or share none at all. The stratification
  is the point of the release: aggregate metrics on this task are carried by the pairs
  that are already string-identical, and blocking never proposes the pairs that are not.
authors:
  - given-names: Harshit
    family-names: Gupta
    affiliation: Independent Researcher
keywords:
  - entity resolution
  - record linkage
  - blocking
  - corporate hierarchy
  - benchmark
  - data integration
  - public procurement
  - master data management
